# infra/.env.example
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `infra/.env` and fill in the values you need:
#
#     cp infra/.env.example infra/.env
#
# `infra/.env` is git-ignored. Compose reads it automatically when you
# run `docker compose up` from `infra/` (or via `-f infra/docker-compose.yml`).
#
# Every variable is optional; the gateway boots and the dashboard works
# without any secret. You only need an entry when:
#   - HF_TOKEN       → faster Hugging Face downloads / rate-limit relief
#   - GATEWAY_URL    → dashboard talks to a non-default gateway
#   - <your-secret>  → see "Target-side credentials" below
#
# ── Hugging Face Hub ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens — read-scope is enough.
HF_TOKEN=

# ── Target-side credentials (user-named, optional) ──────────────────
# Every additional `KEY=value` line in this file becomes an env-var
# inside the gateway container. There is NO fixed set of supported
# providers — you choose the name. A target with
# `auth.token_env: MY_KEY` (or `query_value_env: MY_KEY`) will pick
# up whatever you put under `MY_KEY=...` here.
#
# Preferred path: skip this file entirely and add secrets through the
# dashboard's **Targets** page. They land in a local, git-ignored
# vault and are available without a container restart.
#
# Example (uncomment + adapt — the names are yours to pick):
#   MY_OPENWEBUI_KEY=sk-...
#   MY_OPENAI_KEY=sk-...
#   MY_INTERNAL_BEARER=...

# ── Dashboard wiring (rarely changed) ───────────────────────────────
# Default `http://gateway:8000` works for the in-network case.
# Override only if the dashboard should hit a host-side gateway:
#   GATEWAY_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8000
GATEWAY_URL=
GATEWAY_TIMEOUT_S=120
